    "title": "St. Charles County Fair marches on despite heat - NewsBreak",
    "text": "FORISTELL, Mo. – Despite the heat, attendees flocked to the St. Charles County Fair at Rotary Park on Wednesday, eager to enjoy the summer fun. Thanks for signing up! Watch for us in your inbox. Subscribe Now To ensure everyone stays safe and has a good time, staff at the County Fair have set up cooling tents around the grounds, lined with fans to help people stay cool. One indoor exhibit filled with 4-H and FFA projects also helped attendees beat the heat as they stepped into the air-conditioning. Staff members are also ensuring that the livestock competing in the fair’s judging events won’t become overheated. For example, staff members packed ice bags for the chickens to sit on, made frozen water bottles for the rabbits to snuggle up beside, and consistently provided fans and baths for the cattle. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to FOX 2.",
